From: oveRTOS
Subject: [PATCH] tests/docker: fetch zlib from its GitHub release

The wasm64 cross image downloads zlib from zlib.net, which keeps only
the newest release at its top level.  Once a newer zlib ships, the URL
for the pinned ZLIB_VERSION returns an HTML error page, and tar fails
with "xz: (stdin): File format not recognized".

Fetch the tarball from the GitHub release instead, whose assets stay
in place.  Add -f so an HTTP error fails with curl's message rather
than feeding the error page to tar.

---
--- a/tests/docker/dockerfiles/emsdk-wasm64-cross.docker
+++ b/tests/docker/dockerfiles/emsdk-wasm64-cross.docker
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
 FROM build-base AS zlib-dev
 ARG ZLIB_VERSION
 RUN mkdir -p /zlib
-RUN curl -Ls https://zlib.net/zlib-$ZLIB_VERSION.tar.xz | \
+RUN curl -fsSL https://github.com/madler/zlib/releases/download/v$ZLIB_VERSION/zlib-$ZLIB_VERSION.tar.xz | \
     tar xJC /zlib --strip-components=1
 WORKDIR /zlib
 RUN emconfigure ./configure --prefix=$TARGET --static
